body:
### Bug type

Behavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)

### Beta release blocker

No

### Summary

When setting up OpenClaw via the Windows Companion app, the automated gateway install pipeline fails. The script passes --node-version as Node 22.22.3, which causes install-cli.sh to exit with an error because OpenClaw now enforces Node 24.16.0+ or 26.1.0+.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Launch the latest version of the OpenClaw Windows Companion App on Windows 11.
2. Click Install gateway to begin the automated initial provisioning pipeline. 
3. Observe the failure during the CLI installation step where the installer attempts to execute install-cli.sh with Node 22 (--node-version 22.22.3) instead of Node 24/26.
5. Note that the step exits with code 1, causing the pipeline to abort.

### Expected behavior

The setup pipeline in the Windows Companion App should pass a supported Node version (24.16.0+ or 26.1.0+) when executing install-cli.sh inside the managed WSL container.

### Actual behavior

The setup pipeline aborts during the install-cli step with exit code 1 because install-cli.sh attempts to use unsupported Node version 22.22.3. This causes the installer to output ERROR: Node 22.22.3 is unsupported; use Node 24.16.0+ or Node 26.1.0+ and triggers a complete rollback that unregisters the newly created OpenClawGateway WSL distro.

### OpenClaw version

2026.7.1-4

### Operating system

Windows 11 (25H2)

### Install method

OpenClawCompanion-Setup-x64.exe

### Model

none

### Provider / routing chain

none

### Additional provider/model setup details

_No response_

